cans chose Tom Tiffany. Polling since midsummer consistently shows Crowley ahead, with even Republican-sponsored surveys giving him a three-to-four-point edge among likely voters. Prediction markets put Democratic chances around 80 to 84 percent, and most expert ratings lean Democratic, though several call it a tossup.\n\nTiffany has a major financial advantage, raising over ten million dollars to Crowley's one million, and the race is being contested on affordability, diesel costs, and data centers in an evenly divided state. The evidence favors Crowley modestly, but the spending gap and swing-state volatility keep the race within reach for Republicans.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7127, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7543, "margin": 3.5}]}